From 44a2a907747c01c49efc577eb36fea94b7ebb12b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:36:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: report the Steam Frame controller as itself
 (XR_VALVE_frame_controller_interaction)

A Steam Frame client that has SteamVR's native Frame bindings now says so in the tracking packet
(controllerProfile, with per-input bits and touchState). The runtime then advertises and accepts
/interaction_profiles/valve/frame_controller_valve, reports it as current to an app that suggested
it, and reads each Frame input on its own: A, B, X, Y and menu on the right, the four d-pad
directions and view on the left, and a bumper on each hand. Apps without Frame bindings get Oculus
Touch, as before, with the meaning SteamVR's own Frame-to-Touch remap gives the buttons.

When the Frame profile is current, only its bindings are read: an app that suggests both would
otherwise see Frame X also fire its Touch B action.

The packet grows by gazeDirection (which the Frame client already sends), controllerProfile and
touchState. A packet that stops before the end of touchState carries no profile, so an older client's
padding is never read as one. The USB tracking path no longer drops packets smaller than the struct.

Tests: Frame profile and inputs, Touch fallback meanings, an older client's 1080-byte packet, and the
profile accepted only with its extension enabled.

